 @Lemard77  They are made in China, but are made for NVIDIA which is American company.
Production cost of 4090 is lets say 500$, NVIDIA pays for shipping, customs and taxes and it costs them lets say 800$ total. Then NVIDIA sells their cards to everyone else at their desired MSRP which is in this case 1499$ and they are making 699$ profit per card. 
EU companies cant buy cards directly from factory in China but they have to buy it from NVIDIA. To those companies NVIDIA will give discount depending on how much they buy. (anywhere from 5-30%). That discount will go on MSRP and not on those 800$ that card actually costed NVIDIA and then on those prices EU companies have to pay shipping, customs and taxes.

